From eb8972b76fe635c7dc5ea42efde3714f0855aa49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: juanan <juanan@test.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:36:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] T6: add privacy provider for the IED data

- Graded user: the export (through core_grading) includes the numeric
  grade, criteria without level and the validation history (original and
  validated grade, level, feedback and date) without the identity of the
  teacher or the validator. Deletion removes the history of the instances.
- Teacher and validator: the plugin is also a plugin\provider and
  core_userlist_provider. They get the validations they did or that
  affected their grades; on deletion they are anonymised and the rows are
  kept, so the grade stays validated.
- Metadata for the numeric grade, the validation history and the weights.
- Fix upstream export: LEFT JOIN on levels so criteria without level are
  not lost. The export stays keyed by criterion description as upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
